{% doc %}
  The product categories, read from Admin's navigation — never typed in
  the theme. Prints "handle::label" pairs joined by "||", nothing else,
  so it is used through capture:

    {%- capture raw -%}{% render 'sv-cat-list' %}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign cats = raw | strip | split: '||' -%}
    → each entry split by '::' gives the collection handle and the label

  With `parent`, it prints that category's SUB-categories instead (the
  pikabookidz "Diaper & Nappy → Muslin nappy · Velcro nappy" level).

  ── Where categories come from, in order ──────────────────────────────
  1. A menu with the handle `sv-categories`, if the store has one: its
     top level is the categories, its second level the sub-categories.
  2. Otherwise the main menu's own category entry — the top-level item
     that links to /pages/products, or is titled "Products", "Shop by
     Type", "Shop by Category" or "Categories". Its children are the
     categories and their children the sub-categories.

  Only links that point at a collection count; a page or URL link in the
  same list is skipped, because a category has to have a shelf to land on.

  @param {string} [parent] - Collection handle whose sub-categories to list
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign top = blank
  assign own = linklists['sv-categories']
  if own.links.size > 0
    assign top = own.links
  else
    for link in linklists['main-menu'].links
      assign t = link.title | downcase | strip
      assign u = link.url | downcase
      if u contains '/pages/products' or t == 'products' or t == 'shop by type' or t == 'shop by category' or t == 'categories'
        assign top = link.links
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  assign out = ''
  for link in top
    if link.type != 'collection_link' or link.object == blank
      continue
    endif
    if parent != blank
      if link.object.handle != parent
        continue
      endif
      for sub in link.links
        if sub.type != 'collection_link' or sub.object == blank
          continue
        endif
        assign out = out | append: sub.object.handle | append: '::' | append: sub.title | append: '||'
      endfor
      break
    else
      assign out = out | append: link.object.handle | append: '::' | append: link.title | append: '||'
    endif
  endfor
  echo out
-%}
